<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikola Pašić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikola Pašić was a Serbian statesman and a founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-radical-party">People's Radical Party</a> who served many times as prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>. He led Serbia through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corfu-declaration">Corfu Declaration</a> of 1917 on a union of the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>. In the new kingdom he championed a centralised state dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikola-pasic.jpg" alt="Nikola Pašić" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NikolaPasic--balkancockpitpol00pric_0191.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
